      "AA_052026 72 baseline/support/q-range combinations evaluated\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import itertools\n",
    "rows=[]\n",
    "for name,spec in SPECS.items():\n",
    "    for kind,end,start,qmax in itertools.product(['linear','pre','post'],spec['ends'],spec['starts'],[.15,.25]):\n",
    "        r,_=evaluate(name,kind,end,start,qmax);rows.append(r)\n",
    "    print(name, '72 baseline/support/q-range combinations evaluated')\n",
    "(OUT/'rotation_grid.json').write_text(json.dumps(rows,indent=2));\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1bd2f5ab",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Refit the decomposition under noise; do not treat C as exact\n",
    "Each sample gets 100 parametric perturbations of all 450 original frame profiles, followed by the same residual-background transform and a fresh EFA rotation. The DAT uncertainty column is the standard deviation of these recovered curves. Bootstrap intervals remain conditional on this baseline, component count and supports.\n",
    "\n",
    "A separate 200-replicate rank-one null simulation tests whether the second singular value exceeds what the supplied errors and the new shared baseline could produce. It tests an additional signal pattern, **not oligomer identity**. Error calibration and unmodelled background structure can affect this test."
   ]
  },
